    {
      "text": "Puts enemies to sleep, then eats their dreams. Occasionally gets sick from eating only bad dreams.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you think that you had a good dream but you can’t remember it, a Drowzee has probably eaten it.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that one of these Pokémon is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "If your nose becomes itchy while you are sleeping, it’s a sure sign that one of these Pokémon is standing above your pillow and trying to eat your dream through your nostrils.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "A Pokémon that nourishes itself by eating dreams, it is thought to share common ancestry with Munna and Musharna.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It finds really fun dreams tasty. When it makes friends with people, it may show them the most delicious dreams it’s ever eaten.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It can be spotted near recreational facilities, intending to eat the pleasant dreams of children who enjoyed themselves there that day.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It puts its prey to sleep and devours their dreams. It seems that bad dreams taste sour, so Drowzee doesn’t particularly like eating them.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it had eaten in the past.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "If you sleep by it all the time, it will sometimes show you dreams it had eaten in the past.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    }
